.TH OEC 1
.SH NAME
oec \- OpenEditorCode terminal project editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oec
.RI [ PROJECT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenEditorCode edits UTF-8 project files in a terminal. Without PROJECT it opens the current directory.
.PP
The complete, versioned Spanish manual is installed as docs/manual.md with the npm package. It defines search, ignored paths, configuration, recovery, Git, updates, shortcuts, limits and security guarantees.
.PP
Markdown project files open in a read-only preview by default. Ctrl+Alt+M switches a project Markdown file between preview and source editing. The bundled manual is always read-only. PNG, JPEG, WebP and GIF previews use Kitty or Sixel when supported and otherwise fall back to terminal blocks.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On Windows OEC stores config.json under %APPDATA%\\openeditorcode. On Linux it uses ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/openeditorcode. Invalid or startup-crashing configuration is copied to config.bkp.json and factory defaults are restored.
.SH FILES
.I docs/manual.md
Complete manual.
.br
.I docs/oec-config.schema.json
Configuration schema.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openeditorcode (1)
